1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,954
Wow.
哇。

2
00:00:01,964 --> 00:00:08,350
Thank you.
谢谢你。

3
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:10,203
Thank you, Massachusetts.
谢谢你，马萨诸塞州。

4
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:16,140
I'm I am so happy.
我我真是太幸福了。

5
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:17,420
I'm so humbled.
我真是太谦虚了

6
00:00:17,420 --> 00:00:25,791
And I'm so grateful that you've given me the opportunity to serve as your governor for the next 4 years.
我非常感谢你们给我机会在未来四年担任你们的州长。

7
00:00:25,791 --> 00:00:37,720
And can we just give a big thank you to my friend, my teammate,
我们能否向我的朋友、我的队友致以深深的谢意？

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,565
And the best lieutenant governor in the country, Kim Driscoll?
还有全国最好的副州长金·德里斯科尔（Kim Driscoll）？

9
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:48,950
It's pretty funny.
这很有趣。

10
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:51,810
Can you believe there was talk about not needing a lieutenant governor?
你能相信有人在谈论不需要副州长吗？

11
00:00:55,630 --> 00:01:02,270
To see the people that Kim helps, the houses she gets built, the cities and towns she supports.
看看金帮助的人、她建造的房屋、她支持的城镇。

12
00:01:03,070 --> 00:01:10,070
It should leave no doubt in anyone's mind that Massachusetts doesn't just need a lieutenant governor.
毫无疑问，马萨诸塞州不仅仅需要一位副州长。

13
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:13,630
We need Kim Driscoll.
我们需要金·德里斯科尔。

14
00:01:13,630 --> 00:01:14,380
Thank you, Kim.
谢谢你，金。

15
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:19,750
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

16
00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:20,610
Thank you, Kim.
谢谢你，金。

17
00:01:21,430 --> 00:01:22,930
I am boy.
我是男孩。

18
00:01:23,910 --> 00:01:25,990
I am to Joanna.
我是乔安娜。

19
00:01:27,270 --> 00:01:27,890
To Joanna.
给乔安娜。

20
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:57,350
Joanna, I You're an incredible person.
乔安娜，我你是一个不可思议的人。

21
00:01:57,350 --> 00:02:01,270
Um and I am just so grateful for all that you give to me.
嗯，我非常感谢你给予我的一切。

22
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:09,990
You're an incredible daughter, friend, coach, who also happens to be a really badass ceo of an organization that's saving democracy.
你是一个令人难以置信的女儿、朋友、教练，同时也是一个拯救民主组织的超级首席执行官。

23
00:02:11,937 --> 00:02:25,100
I'm so blessed to be on this journey with you and the kids and to be able to be here together tonight for this.
我很幸运能够与您和孩子们一起踏上这段旅程，并今晚能够聚在这里。

24
00:02:25,218 --> 00:02:26,180
So, thank you.
所以，谢谢你。

25
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,580
Thank you, family.
谢谢你们，家人。

26
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:40,740
I also want to thank my friends, my family, who stood by me and supported me for the last 55 years, Some of them.
我还要感谢我的朋友和家人，他们在过去 55 年里一直支持我，其中一些。

27
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:46,660
Especially to my mom, who taught me that empathy and strength go hand in hand.
尤其是我的妈妈，她教会我同理心和力量是相辅相成的。

28
00:02:47,532 --> 00:02:50,920
And my stepdad, who's always there when I need it most.
还有我的继父，他总是在我最需要的时候出现。

29
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,120
Thank you.
谢谢你。

30
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:53,020
Thank you, family.
谢谢你们，家人。

31
00:02:54,231 --> 00:03:00,960
Thank you to our union men and women.
感谢我们工会的男男女女。

32
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:10,448
You guys, you guys, you take you one of three I Oh, we'll have a competition.
你们，你们，你们三个选一个吧，哦，我们来一场比赛。

33
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:15,300
Listen, union men and women, you take care of people.
听着，工会男女，你们照顾人民。

34
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:16,500
You teach our kids.
你教我们的孩子。

35
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:18,220
You build our buildings.
你建造我们的建筑物。

36
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,600
You drive our trains and buses.
您驾驶我们的火车和公共汽车。

37
00:03:20,780 --> 00:03:23,200
You keep our community safe and so much more.
您维护了我们社区的安全等等。

38
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:29,700
You keep Massachusetts running and you kept this campaign running at full speed the whole way.
你们让马萨诸塞州继续运转，让这场竞选活动全程全速进行。

39
00:03:29,920 --> 00:03:31,780
I'm so grateful to you all.
我非常感谢你们大家。

40
00:03:33,960 --> 00:03:35,300
Thank you, labor.
谢谢你，劳动。

41
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:47,080
I want to thank the absolute best campaign team and volunteers in the country.
我要感谢该国绝对最好的竞选团队和志愿者。

42
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:48,303
And I mean that.
我的意思是。

43
00:03:49,907 --> 00:03:51,004
I mean that.
我的意思是。

44
00:03:51,004 --> 00:03:57,020
And there are a lot of great campaign teams and a lot of great victories tonight.
今晚有很多伟大的竞选团队和很多伟大的胜利。

45
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:01,520
But Kim and I, we have the best campaign team and volunteers in the country.
但是金和我，我们拥有全国最好的竞选团队和志愿者。

46
00:04:06,310 --> 00:04:10,370
You guys built this grassroots campaign.
你们发起了这场草根运动。

47
00:04:10,650 --> 00:04:15,270
You knocked the doors, you made the calls, you created the content that connects,
你敲了门，你拨打了电话，你创建了连接的内容，

48
00:04:15,831 --> 00:04:18,450
And you met people where they are.
你在人们所在的地方遇见了他们。

49
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:21,490
Tonight, you guys brought this race home.
今晚，你们把这场比赛带回家了。

50
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:22,590
Thank you so much.
太感谢了。

51
00:04:22,650 --> 00:04:23,330
You are the best.
你是最棒的。

52
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,030
You are the best.
你是最棒的。

53
00:04:25,930 --> 00:04:32,110
And I hope you stay close to me and to one another.
我希望你们与我和彼此保持亲密关系。

54
00:04:32,410 --> 00:04:32,890
Thank you.
谢谢你。

55
00:04:38,710 --> 00:04:44,170
And to our team in the governor's office and throughout our administration.
还有我们州长办公室和整个政府的团队。

56
00:04:44,928 --> 00:04:51,410
Thank you for answering the call to public service.
感谢您接听公共服务电话。

57
00:04:52,370 --> 00:04:55,650
You get up every single day and make people's lives better.
你每天起床，让人们的生活变得更好。

58
00:04:56,490 --> 00:05:03,390
Now, most of that work will never make headlines, but it always always makes a difference.
现在，大部分工作永远不会成为头条新闻，但它总是会产生影响。

59
00:05:04,110 --> 00:05:05,370
I'm so grateful to you.
我非常感谢你。

60
00:05:06,174 --> 00:05:07,370
And now we've got more to do.
现在我们还有更多工作要做。

61
00:05:08,508 --> 00:05:21,020
Most of all, I want to thank every person across this state who took the time to tell me their stories,
最重要的是，我要感谢本州每一位花时间向我讲述他们的故事的人，

62
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,340
Their joys, their pains, their challenges.
他们的欢乐，他们的痛苦，他们的挑战。

63
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:28,800
I want you to know it's your stories that drive me.
我想让你知道是你的故事激励着我。

64
00:05:30,534 --> 00:05:33,860
Tonight I spoke with an opponent.
今晚我与一位对手交谈。

65
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:34,960
I wished him well.
我祝他一切顺利。

66
00:05:35,694 --> 00:05:40,860
Um and to those who supported my opponents in this race, here's my promise.
嗯，对于那些在这场比赛中支持我的对手的人，这是我的承诺。

67
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:42,700
Here's my promise.
这是我的承诺。

68
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:44,440
I'll show up for you.
我会为你出现。

69
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:46,020
I'll fight for you.
我会为你而战。

70
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:48,500
I'll be a governor for everyone.
我将成为所有人的州长。

71
00:05:55,020 --> 00:06:00,580
Now this looks like it's going to be a really good night for Democrats around the country.
现在看来，对于全国各地的民主党人来说，这将是一个非常美好的夜晚。

72
00:06:01,814 --> 00:06:07,920
And I believe we're going to have a record of Democratic women governors elected as well.
我相信我们也将创造民主党女州长当选的纪录。

73
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:23,460
It looks like we're going to have a great Democratic House led by our fantastic delegation.
看起来我们将拥有一个由我们出色的代表团领导的伟大的民主党众议院。

74
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:28,380
And we may take the United States Senate as well.
我们也可能会选择美国参议院。

75
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:32,440
Congratulations to our great Senator Ed Markey on his victory tonight.
祝贺我们伟大的参议员埃德·马基今晚取得胜利。

76
00:06:33,004 --> 00:06:43,030
I also want to congratulate all the great candidates who've won their races for state representative and senator.
我还要祝贺所有赢得州众议员和参议员竞选的优秀候选人。

77
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:46,610
I look forward to working with each of you to move Massachusetts forward.
我期待与你们每一个人合作，推动马萨诸塞州向前发展。

78
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:58,620
Now, I know there's going to be a lot of political analysis and discussion over the next few days about what this election means.
现在，我知道在接下来的几天里将会有很多关于这次选举意味着什么的政治分析和讨论。

79
00:06:59,855 --> 00:07:01,400
But here's what it means to me.
但这对我来说意味着什么。

80
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:12,207
It means that I have an obligation, a responsibility, to get up every day and to drive change with urgency and action.
这意味着我有义务、有责任每天起床并立即采取行动推动变革。

81
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:14,980
I may not get it right every time.
我可能不会每次都做对。

82
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:21,380
You may disagree with some of the things I make the decisions that I make.
您可能不同意我所做的一些决定。

83
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:23,180
And you should.
你应该这样做。

84
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:33,320
But I promise you this, I'm going to work my hardest every single day for the things that matter in your lives.
但我向你保证，我每天都会为你生活中重要的事情而努力工作。

85
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:43,640
To show up, to deliver, and to stand up when you need it most.
在您最需要的时候出现、交付并挺身而出。

86
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:49,460
Now, that starts with lowering your costs, and it's why we got to keep building housing.
现在，首先要降低成本，这就是我们必须继续建造住房的原因。

87
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:55,620
More homes so that our teachers and our first responders and our veterans can live in the communities they serve.
更多住房，以便我们的教师、急救人员和退伍军人能够生活在他们所服务的社区中。

88
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:59,020
We need to bring in more energy to lower those gas and electric bills.
我们需要引入更多能源来降低天然气和电费。

89
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:03,580
We need to lower the cost of health care for our families and businesses.
我们需要降低家庭和企业的医疗保健成本。

90
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:09,400
We need to expand access to primary care, mental health care, and maternal health care.
我们需要扩大获得初级保健、精神保健和孕产妇保健的机会。

91
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:16,200
We need to protect our kids in a world of social media and our jobs in the face of AI.
我们需要在社交媒体的世界中保护我们的孩子，并在人工智能面前保护我们的工作。

92
00:08:17,057 --> 00:08:26,800
We need to create more jobs and grow our economy to make this a place where our young people can afford to stay and Live and thrive.
我们需要创造更多就业机会并发展经济，使这里成为我们的年轻人能够居住和居住的地方生存并茁壮成长。

93
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:33,900
And we need this while always protecting your rights and freedoms.
我们需要这一点，同时始终保护您的权利和自由。

94
00:08:35,490 --> 00:08:39,820
I know there's a lot of uncertainty right now.
我知道现在有很多不确定性。

95
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:46,660
But one thing I'm certain of is that the people of Massachusetts, we will meet this moment.
但我确信的一件事是，马萨诸塞州的人民，我们将在这一刻见面。

96
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:48,980
We will meet this moment.
我们将在这一刻相遇。

97
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:51,980
I think about this summer.
我想到了这个夏天。

98
00:08:52,180 --> 00:08:52,620
Here's why.
原因如下。

99
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:54,180
I think about this summer.
我想到了这个夏天。

100
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:56,900
We welcomed the world to Massachusetts.
我们欢迎世界来到马萨诸塞州。

101
00:08:57,397 --> 00:09:00,940
We hosted the World Cup and the tall ships.
我们主办了世界杯和高大的船只。

102
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:08,820
We celebrated the 250th birthday of our country right in the place where American democracy was born.
我们在美国民主诞生的地方庆祝了我们国家的 250 岁生日。

103
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:17,640
So was America's first public school, a rocket ship, and medical breakthroughs that have saved millions of lives around the world.
美国第一所公立学校、一艘火箭飞船以及挽救了全世界数百万人生命的医学突破也是如此。

104
00:09:18,297 --> 00:09:25,800
Because for centuries, the people of Massachusetts have sparked the change the world has needed to see.
因为几个世纪以来，马萨诸塞州人民引发了世界需要看到的变革。

105
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:31,340
They've shown courage, they've shown resilience, and they've shown compassion in the face of challenge.
他们在面对挑战时表现出了勇气、韧性和同情心。

106
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:35,420
That's because in Massachusetts, we lead.
那是因为在马萨诸塞州，我们处于领先地位。

107
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:36,460
We don't follow.
我们不跟随。

108
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:48,010
And tonight, tonight, you chose the kind of state we want to be.
今晚，今晚，你选择了我们想要的状态。

109
00:09:49,217 --> 00:09:55,130
A state and a place where everyone can live free and safe in their communities,
一个每个人都可以在自己的社区自由、安全生活的州和地方，

110
00:09:55,750 --> 00:10:05,170
Where diversity is a strength, not a flaw, where families can thrive, and where there's no better place to raise a child,
多样性是一种优势，而不是缺点，家庭可以蓬勃发展，没有更好的地方可以养育孩子，

111
00:10:05,670 --> 00:10:11,550
Where we nourish our kids and give them an education that sets them up for success,
我们滋养我们的孩子并为他们提供帮助他们走向成功的教育，

112
00:10:11,550 --> 00:10:13,830
No matter their career path.
无论他们的职业道路如何。

113
00:10:13,830 --> 00:10:19,830
Where we make sure our seniors get housing and health care that they deserve.
我们确保我们的老年人获得他们应得的住房和医疗保健。

114
00:10:20,390 --> 00:10:22,750
Where we champion science and research.
我们在这里倡导科学和研究。

115
00:10:23,350 --> 00:10:31,390
Where someone with an idea and a little bit of determination can start a small business or incubate the next Vertex.
拥有想法和一点决心的人可以创办一家小企业或孵化下一个 Vertex。

116
00:10:32,010 --> 00:10:36,090
Where young people know they can be who they are and be proud of it.
年轻人知道他们可以成为自己，并为此感到自豪。

117
00:10:36,730 --> 00:10:41,870
And where women make decisions about their own health care, not the government.
女性而不是政府对自己的医疗保健做出决定。

118
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:58,800
Tonight Tonight's a moment of hope and of action.
今晚 今晚是充满希望和行动的时刻。

119
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:00,520
Hope and action.
希望和行动。

120
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:04,620
That's what Kim Driscoll and I are all about.
这就是我和金·德里斯科尔所做的一切。

121
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:09,540
And that's what the next four years are going to be about.
这就是未来四年的目标。

122
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:15,020
So let's celebrate tonight and in the morning, we're going to get back to work.
所以让我们今晚庆祝一下，明天早上我们就回去工作了。

123
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:16,740
I am so proud to be your governor.
我很自豪能够成为你们的州长。

124
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:18,140
Thank you, Massachusetts.
谢谢你们，马萨诸塞州的人民。
